  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 6.99,
      "end": 16.99,
      "text": "Zero to half, it is past ten. The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1. Hi and welcome to listeners who've just joined us on VHF in glorious, delightful stereo. How are you tonight? I hope you're okay and enjoying the weather.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.99,
      "end": 22.99,
      "text": "I think the weather here is astonishing. I've just spent a couple of weeks in Ibiza and the weather's just about as good as it is in Ibiza. It's wonderful here.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.99,
      "end": 32.99,
      "text": "Right, in the next couple of hours we've got two sessions for you, a repeat of the session we put out not that long ago by Baby Taku and the radio debut of a group from Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.99,
      "end": 34.65,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm stumbling over my words here.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.03,
      "end": 36.83,
      "text": "A group from Scotland called Garrison.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.07,
      "end": 42.15,
      "text": "We've got some new releases by Boxer Frogs, Deanna, Roger Taylor, Little Steven, Fastway, Silhouette,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.59,
      "end": 44.69,
      "text": "and also we have the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.93,
      "end": 46.27,
      "text": "We start, though, with Dio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.33,
      "end": 56.33,
      "text": "That was Gillan from an album that came out on BBC Records back in 1980.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.33,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 813.77,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 816.59,
      "end": 818.61,
      "text": "The album was called Metal Explosion.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 818.77,
      "end": 820.01,
      "text": "The track was called If You Believe Me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 820.01,
      "end": 826.61,
      "text": "And I had a letter from Paul Barton in Glasgow asking why that version is different to the version that is actually on, I think, the album Glory Road.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 828.92,
      "end": 830.02,
      "text": "Well, the story goes like this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 830.08,
      "end": 831.68,
      "text": "I just happened to be in Kingsway Recorders,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 831.84,
      "end": 834.14,
      "text": "which was Ian's recording studio at one time,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 834.2,
      "end": 835.26,
      "text": "and I happened to hear that.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 835.32,
      "end": 836.88,
      "text": "That was more or less a sort of demo version.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 837.52,
      "end": 838.34,
      "text": "And I said to Ian,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 838.38,
      "end": 840.48,
      "text": "boy, I'd really like a copy of that to play on the radio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 840.58,
      "end": 842.22,
      "text": "And he said, there you go, my son, there's the tape.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 842.32,
      "end": 843.46,
      "text": "Enjoy it, love it, there you go.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 843.52,
      "end": 844.12,
      "text": "That was just like that.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 844.24,
      "end": 846.34,
      "text": "He gave me the tape, and it ended up on that album,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 846.72,
      "end": 848.1,
      "text": "which is a Friday Rock Show album.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 848.26,
      "end": 850.5,
      "text": "We're thinking about putting out more records in the future as well,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 850.56,
      "end": 852.18,
      "text": "which I hope you'll be happy to hear,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 852.18,
      "end": 855.36,
      "text": "featuring some of the good music that we put together in session form.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 855.36,
      "end": 858.24,
      "text": "So that was for Paul Barton, who's in Glasgow",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 858.24,
      "end": 859.26,
      "text": "Now you know the story",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 859.26,
      "end": 861.2,
      "text": "Before that, Dio",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 861.2,
      "end": 864.18,
      "text": "And the latest single, which is called We Rock",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 864.18,
      "end": 868.78,
      "text": "17 minutes after 10, a mention here for a fellow by the name of Bill Dutton",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 868.78,
      "end": 871.3,
      "text": "In Bishopsdown, Salisbury and Wiltshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 871.3,
      "end": 874.88,
      "text": "He says he hopes I had a good holiday, and I certainly did",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 874.88,
      "end": 876.96,
      "text": "Thank you, Bill, and I hope you're all right as well, mate",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 876.96,
      "end": 881.29,
      "text": "This is Van Stevenson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 881.29,
      "end": 887.89,
      "text": "The session was first put out on this program last April",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 887.89,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 1322.43,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1322.43,
      "end": 1325.13,
      "text": "They are Baby Taku, the track you heard was called Hot Wheels",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1325.13,
      "end": 1329.55,
      "text": "And before that, Van Stevenson, a single that's out on the MCA record label here in the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1329.99,
      "end": 1331.83,
      "text": "It is called Modern Day Delilah.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1332.03,
      "end": 1332.95,
      "text": "It is 10.25.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1333.25,
      "end": 1335.77,
      "text": "This is the first of three by Garrison from Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1336.71,
      "end": 1346.91,
      "text": "That's a track from a really excellent LP that's just come out on the Epic record label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1346.91,
      "end": 1855.18,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1855.18,
      "end": 1860.78,
      "text": "The name of the band are The Fogs, and The Fogs are John Fiddler, ex-Medicine Head, and also British Lions.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1860.88,
      "end": 1867.0,
      "text": "Methinks, Jim McCarty, Chris Drager, and Paul Samuel Smith, who were all original members of the Yardbirds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1867.88,
      "end": 1870.88,
      "text": "Also playing guitar on that track, which was called The Edge, was Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1872.4,
      "end": 1874.3,
      "text": "The track you just heard was called The Edge.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1874.42,
      "end": 1877.08,
      "text": "The album is Box of Frogs by The Frogs on Epic.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1877.74,
      "end": 1878.72,
      "text": "Well recommended.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1880.1,
      "end": 1883.2,
      "text": "Before that, Gallison, the first of three from our debut session by them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1883.34,
      "end": 1884.48,
      "text": "It was called The First Time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1885.64,
      "end": 1886.6,
      "text": "25 minutes to 11.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1886.8,
      "end": 1889.54,
      "text": "Here's a little card from somebody who signs themselves Triffid.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1890.16,
      "end": 1891.46,
      "text": "Don't you grow in my garden, mate.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1891.68,
      "end": 1893.46,
      "text": "Dear Tom, give a hand to the Norton Headbangers",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1894.04,
      "end": 1897.4,
      "text": "who are going to go and see and hear ACDC at Dunnington Park this year.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1897.4,
      "end": 1905.18,
      "text": "Especially Four Eyes, Blob, Worcester, Jim, Mills, T-Boy, and of course, Triffid",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1905.18,
      "end": 1907.92,
      "text": "The fellow who signs himself Phil Mogg",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1907.92,
      "end": 1910.36,
      "text": "Not the real Phil Mogg",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1910.36,
      "end": 1913.68,
      "text": "Lives up there in Countess Wells Road in Aberdeen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1913.68,
      "end": 1919.16,
      "text": "Says, could you please tell me if and where I can get hold of Radio 1 Rock Show Themes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1919.16,
      "end": 1921.54,
      "text": "It was an EP that was put out, I think, on Polydor Records",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1921.54,
      "end": 1922.7,
      "text": "Is it still available?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1923.46,
      "end": 1926.32,
      "text": "To the best of my knowledge, Phil Mogg of Aberdeen, it's deleted",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1926.32,
      "end": 1930.86,
      "text": "You might find it in a sort of second-hand shop somewhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1930.86,
      "end": 1936.96,
      "text": "From the Frogs to Spider.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1936.96,
      "end": 1942.36,
      "text": "That's a new band that features Mr. Paul D'Anno,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1942.36,
      "end": 2359.18,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2359.18,
      "end": 2361.18,
      "text": "who was the original singer with Iron Maiden.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2361.18,
      "end": 2363.18,
      "text": "Indeed, the singer on their first two albums.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2363.18,
      "end": 2365.18,
      "text": "Now the band that he's in is called D'Anno.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2365.18,
      "end": 2367.18,
      "text": "So indeed is the album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2367.18,
      "end": 2369.18,
      "text": "It's out on the FM record label in the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2369.18,
      "end": 2371.18,
      "text": "The track was called Road Rat.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2371.18,
      "end": 2373.98,
      "text": "Good luck, Paul.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2373.98,
      "end": 2375.98,
      "text": "Have to go for it this time and get it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2375.98,
      "end": 2377.98,
      "text": "And before that, the new single by Spider out on A&M.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2377.98,
      "end": 2379.98,
      "text": "It's called Breakaway.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2379.98,
      "end": 2384.62,
      "text": "The Spider Triad was for two, let me quote it accurately here,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2385.12,
      "end": 2389.36,
      "text": "for two brilliant, young, beautiful ladies by the names of Pam and Babs,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2389.76,
      "end": 2393.92,
      "text": "who pleasingly came to talk to a gentleman by the name of Colin Minnette of Skegby,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2394.44,
      "end": 2395.82,
      "text": "Sutton in Asheville, Nottinghamshire,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2396.4,
      "end": 2400.28,
      "text": "at a pub called the Mason's Arms in Mansfield on Saturday the 19th of May.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2400.98,
      "end": 2404.26,
      "text": "Please tell them, Tom, that I really would love to meet them both again in the same pub",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2404.26,
      "end": 2406.68,
      "text": "any Saturday night, because I owe them a drink.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2407.59,
      "end": 2409.17,
      "text": "There you go, girls and invitations.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2409.17,
      "end": 2412.12,
      "text": "Happy birthday to Brian out of Spider",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2412.12,
      "end": 2414.38,
      "text": "his birthday is next Wednesday the 11th of July",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2414.38,
      "end": 2416.32,
      "text": "same date as me but I'm a bit older",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2416.32,
      "end": 2418.02,
      "text": "Spider on tour at the moment",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2418.02,
      "end": 2419.84,
      "text": "doing 35 dates around the country",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2419.84,
      "end": 2422.33,
      "text": "congratulations to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2422.33,
      "end": 2424.69,
      "text": "Virginia Weatherall for getting her degree",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2424.69,
      "end": 2426.19,
      "text": "and hello to everybody",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2426.19,
      "end": 2428.55,
      "text": "at 47 Lambert Street",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2428.55,
      "end": 2429.21,
      "text": "in Hull",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2429.21,
      "end": 2431.21,
      "text": "lots of love from Claire",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2431.21,
      "end": 2437.21,
      "text": "half an hour to 11 that is my old fist",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2437.21,
      "end": 2911.01,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2909.49,
      "end": 2911.83,
      "text": "and a track from an album that came out in 1981",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2911.83,
      "end": 2913.41,
      "text": "it was on the A&M record label",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2913.41,
      "end": 2916.01,
      "text": "the album was called Thunder in the Rock",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2916.01,
      "end": 2917.93,
      "text": "and the track you heard there was called Evil Cold",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2917.93,
      "end": 2919.97,
      "text": "and I played it because I just found a letter the other day",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2919.97,
      "end": 2922.27,
      "text": "that was sent in something like 11 months ago",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2922.27,
      "end": 2924.05,
      "text": "it got hidden somewhere, I don't know what happened to it",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2924.05,
      "end": 2926.39,
      "text": "a letter from a fellow by the name of Adrian Smith",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2926.39,
